Based on the provided Standard Operating Procedure (SOP) documents, here is the step-by-step procedure on how to start the compressor:

### 1. Pre-Start Checks and Preparation
*   **Inspect Levels & Connections:** Check the engine oil level, radiator water level, battery condition, and self-starter connections. Use an aluminum ladder specifically to check the radiator water level. **[Source 1]**
*   **Check Battery Tightness:** Ensure the battery connections are tight. **[Source 3]**
*   **Position Valves:** Keep the positive isolation valve turned **OFF** and ensure the air delivery/discharge valve is **closed**. **[Source 1, Source 3]**
*   **Secure Doors and Area:** Close the side doors of the engine before starting. Do not allow any unauthorized persons to stand nearby. **[Source 3]**
*   **Wear PPE:** Put on safety helmets, hand gloves, safety shoes, and safety glasses to prevent injuries from slipping or falling doors. **[Source 1]**
*   **Isolation Switch:** Turn ON the positive isolation switch (to prevent accidental starting by anyone else). **[Source 1]**

### 2. Starting Procedure
*   **Ignition & Startup:** Turn the ignition switch **ON**, and then press the starting switch. **[Source 1]**
*   **Engage Loading:** Once the engine oil pressure reaches **4 kg/cm²**, press the loading switch. **[Source 1]**
*   **Warm-up:** Let the compressor run for **5 minutes** to warm up the compressor oil. **[Source 1]**
*   **Safety Warning:** Do not inspect or check any mechanical parts while the compressor is running. **[Source 3]**

### 3. Post-Start Inspection and Operation
*   **Leakage Check:** Inspect the unit for any leaks or abnormalities after starting. **[Source 1]**
*   **Pressure Gauge Check:** Verify the air pressure on the panel board gauge. It should show **10 kg/cm²**. **[Source 3]**
*   **Discharge Valve Operation:** Slowly open the discharge valve and verify the pressure. The pressure in this state must be a minimum of **4 kg/cm²**. Ensure absolutely no one is standing directly in front of the discharge valve. **[Source 3]**

